WEBVTT

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:10.780
So Ra No Wo To

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:43.870
Ready, my little chickens?

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.950
Prepare to advance! Forward!

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.250
Forward!

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.000
Where are our allies?

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.250
Forty degrees, left.
Prepare to fire main cannon!

00:01:58.070 --> 00:01:59.110
Range 400!

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:02.030
Load shell. Type: heat round!

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.060
On it!

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:04.990
Origa!

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.120
Don't worry.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:10.060
I've been locked in this thing for three days.
I'm not dying till we can take a shower.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:12.690
Main gun aimed!

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:13.770
Fire!

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.020
Direct hit!

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:25.320
Anna, report to the rear:

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:28.440
"One tank destroyed.
Continue the advance!"

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:29.300
Roger that!

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.800
Filicia, back her up.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.090
Y-Yes!

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.760
I know it's flashing.
But it isn't lightning, so don't worry.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.630
I know!

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:50.730
Th-Three o'clock!

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.760
No...

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.450
Lieutenant Anna!

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:43.380
<i>Kamiya...</i>

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:50.500
<i>Higoya...</i>

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:22.530
Chirping Crickets -
Spirits Down the River

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:29.030
Hey, Noël! Put your back into it,
or they won't get clean!

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.060
It's so hot out there...

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:59.460
It's cold in the winter, but I love how
cool this building is in the summer.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:03.330
Huh? Aren't Filicia and Rio-sempai
on cleaning duty today?

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:06.570
They said they were busy,
and asked us to do it.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:07.570
Whose is that?

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:09.310
That's Filicia-san's.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:13.080
She said she wasn't hungry,
so we could eat it.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.330
Then I guess I will!

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:20.190
What's that?

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:22.200
Are you preparing dinner?

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.200
Also...

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.210
What are you doing?

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.840
You'll be written up for
playing with the food!

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.330
I'm not playing!

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.240
It's almost time for Obon, isn't it?

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:34.050
Huh? What's Obon?

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.150
Fiesta des Lumières.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:37.690
Fi...

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:42.570
Fiesta des Lumières is a holiday
unique to southern Helvetia.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.440
It originated from a folk religion
that believed that,

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:48.990
for a specific period of time during the summer,
the dead return to the world of the living.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:53.830
Floating paper lanterns down
the river sends them back.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:58.820
In some places, this festival is called Obon.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.080
Here you go!

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.660
Thanks.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:07.330
Huh? So it's the same thing!

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:09.800
Spirits returning...

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:11.200
Wait! Wait!

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:11.970
What?

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.020
Does that mean we'll see ghosts?

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.330
In a way.

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:19.360
Paper lanterns... How wonderful!

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.900
We used to make fires and
stuff back home, but-

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:22.930
No!

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:25.980
The dead go to Heaven
and stay there forever.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:28.530
Only bad things are stuck
wandering the earth!

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:31.160
That's not true!

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.170
But in church...

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.210
We're back!

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:37.200
Come and give us a hand!

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:41.130
Hey, when did you go shopping?

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.000
Those...

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.570
They looked tasty,
so we bought them.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.010
This too.

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:57.660
Will this do?

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:59.740
No, Father!

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:01.190
Do it like this!

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.110
I'm done!

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.900
Your mom and dad?

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.500
I see.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.650
They look great!

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:14.700
What? Even the church is in on it?

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.410
This Fie-thingy?

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.550
Yes.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.330
The Central Orthodox Church
would be up in arms over it,

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.990
but we're in the middle
of nowhere.

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:23.540
They're not very serious.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.640
In my town,

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:29.090
we would make horses and cows

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:32.010
out of cucumbers and eggplants
for our ancestors to ride.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:39.300
And we all danced to
make them happy!

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:43.750
Are you going to make some, too?

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:47.260
Yeah. Last year, we just watched, but...

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:03.900
It's part of our job to maintain
good relations with the locals.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:08.050
If you don't really think about it,
it's just a nice little festival.

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.420
Right, Filicia?

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:25.710
Filicia-san!

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:34.230
Are you OK?

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:35.550
Does it hurt?

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.600
No. I'm fine.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:39.320
I just screwed up a bit.

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:43.350
But you don't make mistakes
like that often.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:44.980
You're not Kanata.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:50.700
You know how hot it's been
these last few days...

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:53.360
I haven't really been
able to sleep.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.740
I'll go take a break.

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:03.570
Filicia-san...

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:07.090
She's acting kind of strange.

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:12.260
She didn't eat her lunch, and she
blew off work to buy watermelons...

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:15.670
She's got a lot on her mind.

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:20.550
I think I'll go talk to her...

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:21.390
Stop!

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:26.190
There are some things she
doesn't want anyone to know!

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:27.910
Leave her alone.

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:32.260
Noël.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:34.930
Do you know about it, Rio?

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.760
I read the records.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:39.440
I know about it first-hand.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:40.450
So...

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:57.170
Filicia...

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:05.890
Keep it steady. Like that.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.330
OK, there's a good girl.

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:18.120
And then there was a monster
that looked just like the captain!

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:29.130
It's hard to believe there used to be
all kinds of living things in this sea.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:32.400
Did you ever hear...

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:39.550
That the world is slowly ending,
and someday there will be no humans.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:43.430
That's just a rumor...

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:51.040
But if it's true, then what
are we fighting for?

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:07.540
I'm still alive...

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.460
Ideograms?

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:50.670
I'm sorry.

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:55.640
I wish I were able to read
your last words...

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:59.200
This equipment...

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:03.570
Is it from the old era?

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:17.440
Captain...

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.730
Lieutenant Origa.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.260
Martina.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.610
Anna-san...

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:27.780
Why am I the only one left...

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:34.750
Why... are you crying?

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:37.280
I see.

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:42.750
There are still survivors
in this world.

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:44.920
I'm sorry.

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:50.800
I'm really sorry.

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:54.800
Why are you apologizing?

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:59.370
Because we lost...

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:03.320
To them.

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:06.570
We couldn't protect you.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.760
I'm truly sorry.

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:30.890
The world ended.

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:33.000
No...

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.700
You're just the last remnant.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:40.140
A few remaining bubbles on
the surface of the water.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:42.770
Humanity...

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:48.180
The world can never regain
the glory it once had.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:50.330
Don't try to decide that for us!

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:52.610
But it's the truth.

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:56.310
So end it.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:05.930
It must be far too painful, living a miserable
life in a world filled with despair.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:07.830
No... No!

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:08.920
Why not?

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:13.510
Is there some meaning to survival
in a world like this?

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.090
I...

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:40.250
Save me...

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:49.660
I'm in here!

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:50.640
I'm alive!

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:51.680
Please!

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.940
Come save me!

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.080
You're...

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:20.610
I'm sorry.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:27.710
If my squad had only arrived half a day earlier,
this never would have happened.

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:30.960
Your Highness, Princess Iria...

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.260
But I was surprised.

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:40.570
At what?

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:45.270
Last year, you ignored the
Fiesta des Lumières.

00:16:45.510 --> 00:16:47.570
What changed?

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.780
Well...

00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:55.460
Pretty colors, huh?

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:57.030
It's made in Treize.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:59.280
I bought it at the last market.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.670
Wow!

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:04.290
It's so wonderful!

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:05.340
Isn't it?

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:12.710
It's true. They used to
be everything to me.

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:18.490
I wanted to protect the country,
the people, like they did.

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.300
But sometimes, I think...

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:25.580
What's the point?

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:32.320
So if they've really come back,

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:34.820
I wanted them to tell me.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.760
But what about you?

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.200
Everyone's worried.

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:46.990
That's true. I may have
made them worry.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:48.870
I failed as a captain.

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:50.860
It's not just them!

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:52.040
I...

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:53.360
Uh...

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:54.350
You?

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:59.210
Anyway, don't try and carry
it all on your own!

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:02.180
At the least, even I can listen to you!

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:03.840
Thank you, Rio.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.770
I'll honor that and tell you, then.

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.050
What is it?

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:09.420
You see...

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:14.770
I've gotten fatter this summer!

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:15.610
What?!

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:18.820
If I don't start losing weight, I won't be
able to fit into my winter clothes.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:21.850
I heard that if you only eat watermelon,
you'll lose weight,

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:23.970
so I thought I'd try it.

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:26.460
What's wrong, Rio?

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.300
Stop it already!

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:33.960
What happened at
the Vingt front...

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:39.440
Oh! Did you think I was
remembering that?

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:42.570
You... You weren't?

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:49.270
It's so pretty!

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:52.230
Shall we go, too?

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:10.000
So you made one, too,
Kureha-chan?

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:13.520
I-I don't believe in
souls and stuff!

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:15.300
It's a mission.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:19.130
Umm... Who are you sending, Filicia-san?

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.490
My old friends

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:26.140
and a soldier whose
name I don't know.

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:30.270
The people who made me realize
something important.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:32.100
Could those people be...

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:34.660
Filicia-san,

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:37.120
if something's bothering
you or anything...

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:38.650
I...

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:43.490
I may not be able to help... But!

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:48.050
It looks like I worried you.

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:49.510
I'm sorry.

00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:52.040
But I'm all right.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.880
That's too sad.

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:56.760
I want to worry for you, too!

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:00.650
You always worry about me!

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:02.600
I always do things to
make you worry.

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:04.740
I want to worry about you!

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:09.060
I love you!

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:15.020
I love you too, Kana-chan.

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:20.000
Stay as you are. Won't you?

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:22.590
Filicia-san.

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:25.400
What you're always teaching me,

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:29.290
to not fear putting your
feelings into words...

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:33.450
I think that's wonderful.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:38.780
Captain.

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:45.090
Filicia... Me, too.

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:51.830
Guys...

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.350
You're all so cute.

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:07.620
Come back next year, ancestors.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:16.130
Dad... Mom...

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:29.640
Mother... Sister...

00:21:30.590 --> 00:21:32.520
That girl is...

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:42.230
Hey, Rio. You were asking if there
was some meaning in this world.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:43.250
Yeah.

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:48.880
When I was the only one who survived,
it was all I could think about.

00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:52.290
Why had I, alone, survived?

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:56.040
What did it mean?

00:21:56.390 --> 00:21:58.110
And I realized,

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:02.800
I'm sure there's no meaning
in this world.

00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:07.050
But isn't that wonderful?

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:13.620
That means you can
find your own.

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:19.830
And I've found mine.

00:22:20.570 --> 00:22:22.850
The meaning to my being here...

00:22:23.860 --> 00:22:26.420
And then the priest...

00:22:26.420 --> 00:22:27.710
What about him?

00:22:27.710 --> 00:22:30.090
Well, he was super selfish,
so Yumina-neechan...

00:22:30.090 --> 00:22:31.870
What?!

00:22:32.630 --> 00:22:38.260
I don't want them to
suffer like I did.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:40.440
Yeah...

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:19.930
Phone Duty - We Have an Emergency

00:24:15.750 --> 00:24:16.710
Next time:

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:17.400
Phone Duty.

00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:19.340
We Have an Emergency!

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:24.930
This program is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to people, parties,
or situations is purely coincidental.
